Scripted.

1480
01:03:40.020 --> 01:03:40.420
Beautiful.

1481
01:03:40.920 --> 01:03:41.920
So, so good.

1482
01:03:42.180 --> 01:03:45.360
What wasn't in the script was, I am irate right now.

1483
01:03:46.240 --> 01:03:47.520
That was not in the script.

1484
01:03:48.040 --> 01:03:53.020
And there were a couple of other little lines, but they were always just like a play on what

1485
01:03:53.020 --> 01:03:53.980
was already there.

1486
01:03:54.160 --> 01:03:54.380
Right.

1487
01:03:54.580 --> 01:03:57.080
But yeah, that scene is just beautiful.

1488
01:03:57.940 --> 01:04:02.260
Next is a scene that we didn't talk about with Stephen, and I wish we had.

1489
01:04:02.260 --> 01:04:07.500
And it's that moment when Dwight peels his car out and tells Jim to get in.

1490
01:04:07.680 --> 01:04:08.700
Jenna, I know.

1491
01:04:08.840 --> 01:04:10.240
I meant to ask him about it.

1492
01:04:10.400 --> 01:04:15.880
So he talked about it in the DVD commentary that he loved how absurd it was that Dwight

1493
01:04:15.880 --> 01:04:19.180
was like, get in, and then peels out, and you really think they're going to just tear

1494
01:04:19.180 --> 01:04:20.640
out of the parking lot and go somewhere.

1495
01:04:20.780 --> 01:04:21.660
And then they go nowhere.

1496
01:04:21.780 --> 01:04:25.100
And then he wanted him to make like a hard left and just go into his parking spot.

1497
01:04:25.220 --> 01:04:25.900
And Jim's like, what?

1498
01:04:26.400 --> 01:04:29.280
And Stephen said he wanted it to be even bigger.

1499
01:04:29.440 --> 01:04:31.340
He was like, can we do an even bigger peel out?

1500
01:04:31.340 --> 01:04:33.080
But there just wasn't the space.

1501
01:04:33.460 --> 01:04:38.980
Well, I found this interview with Lester where he said that originally they were just

1502
01:04:38.980 --> 01:04:42.300
going to have them meet, that Dwight was just going to have them meet down in the parking

1503
01:04:42.300 --> 01:04:46.780
lot, and they were going to have this conversation, and that Stephen pitched, oh, guys, let's

1504
01:04:46.780 --> 01:04:49.380
make it more interesting and do this crazy car maneuver.

1505
01:04:49.680 --> 01:04:50.720
It's so funny.

1506
01:04:50.880 --> 01:04:52.240
So, so, so funny.

1507
01:04:52.480 --> 01:04:55.180
I did get a fan catch from Madeline R.

1508
01:04:55.700 --> 01:04:59.160
She is pretty sure that Pam's car is in the parking

1509
01:04:59.160 --> 01:04:59.460
lot.

1510
01:05:00.060 --> 01:05:01.480
Oh, that's a good catch.

1511
01:05:01.500 --> 01:05:02.220
In this scene.

1512
01:05:02.520 --> 01:05:05.260
So I looked for it, and it's so faSt.

1513
01:05:05.260 --> 01:05:06.580
I couldn't register it.

1514
01:05:06.680 --> 01:05:09.240
But I bet, you know, they just would leave our cars there.

1515
01:05:09.560 --> 01:05:09.880
Yeah.

1516
01:05:10.220 --> 01:05:12.220
So I think there's a good chance it's there.

1517
01:05:12.360 --> 01:05:13.160
Oh, for sure.

1518
01:05:13.160 --> 01:05:13.680
I bet.

1519
01:05:14.120 --> 01:05:17.920
Well, you know, one of the things I loved about this scene was Dwight is, you know,

1520
01:05:18.000 --> 01:05:20.280
convinced someone might be listening into their conversation.

1521
01:05:20.580 --> 01:05:24.040
So he plays Jay Giles' band, the song Centerfold.

1522
01:05:24.160 --> 01:05:24.360
Yeah.

1523
01:05:24.360 --> 01:05:24.980
Really loud.

1524
01:05:25.260 --> 01:05:26.360
It just took me back.

1525
01:05:26.480 --> 01:05:27.740
I'm like, where are my roller skates?

1526
01:05:29.180 --> 01:05:31.280
I went and listened to the album last night.

1527
01:05:31.440 --> 01:05:36.500
And you guys, if you haven't watched music videos from this time, go back.

1528
01:05:36.660 --> 01:05:37.440
They're pretty special.

1529
01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:38.360
They're real special.

1530
01:05:38.620 --> 01:05:39.220
They're delightful.

1531
01:05:39.540 --> 01:05:41.500
My kids were like, what are they doing?

1532
01:05:41.720 --> 01:05:43.440
I'm like, you guys, this is a music video.

1533
01:05:43.680 --> 01:05:44.560
Oh, my gosh.

1534
01:05:44.560 --> 01:05:47.280
I remember watching music videos on MTV.

1535
01:05:47.820 --> 01:05:50.920
And then do you remember the VH1 pop-up thing?

1536
01:05:51.180 --> 01:05:51.480
Yeah.

1537
01:05:51.640 --> 01:05:53.540
Where they would pop up little facts on the screen?

1538
01:05:53.760 --> 01:05:54.700
Yeah, I loved those.

1539
01:05:54.840 --> 01:05:55.280
Me too.

1540
01:05:55.600 --> 01:05:57.900
Our whole generation grew up watching music videos.

1541
01:05:58.080 --> 01:05:58.420
Mm-hmm.

1542
01:05:58.560 --> 01:05:59.200
It's wild.

1543
01:05:59.760 --> 01:06:06.020
So now we're back in the office, and Dwight is on a sales call, but he becomes increasingly

1544
01:06:06.020 --> 01:06:08.420
convinced that someone is listening to him.

1545
01:06:08.420 --> 01:06:16.260
He's talking to a guy on the phone who, by the way, I found out, was played by actor

1546
01:06:16.260 --> 01:06:21.100
Steve Zissis, who, if you don't know who he is, he is amazing.

1547
01:06:21.420 --> 01:06:26.460
He is one of the stars of the movie Baghead, which he made with the Duplass brothers.

1548
01:06:26.780 --> 01:06:33.040
Then he went on to create the TV comedy Togetherness with them, and he has a story by credit on the

1549
01:06:33.040 --> 01:06:34.120
new film Cruella.

1550
01:06:34.420 --> 01:06:37.740
I mean, he's part of that whole, like, mumblecore movement.

1551
01:06:37.740 --> 01:06:41.320
We got the best actors just to be voices on the phone.

1552
01:06:41.460 --> 01:06:42.040
What the hell?

1553
01:06:42.240 --> 01:06:42.900
What the heck?

1554
01:06:43.380 --> 01:06:44.480
Dwight is positive.

1555
01:06:44.640 --> 01:06:47.220
It's Kelly, and he charges back there, right?

1556
01:06:47.600 --> 01:06:48.040
Yes.

1557
01:06:48.460 --> 01:06:51.860
And he finds her on the phone, and she's like, you can't just come into my nook and call

1558
01:06:51.860 --> 01:06:52.340
me stupid.

1559
01:06:52.640 --> 01:06:53.500
Get out of my nook.

1560
01:06:53.620 --> 01:06:57.760
And then Pam, over at the corporate offices, goes, that's what she said!

1561
01:06:57.800 --> 01:06:58.600
That's what she said!

1562
01:06:59.520 --> 01:07:03.240
Okay, that was an improvised pitch by John Krasinski.

1563
01:07:03.500 --> 01:07:04.280
Oh, cute!

1564
01:07:04.280 --> 01:07:08.840
So I'm there, and John is like, oh my gosh, it should be a, that's what she said, that's

1565
01:07:08.840 --> 01:07:09.460
what she said!

1566
01:07:09.580 --> 01:07:14.740
And so we did it, we saved it, and then when I went to the corporate offices, we shot my

1567
01:07:14.740 --> 01:07:15.280
side of it.

1568
01:07:15.400 --> 01:07:17.060
That is so cute, I love that.

1569
01:07:17.700 --> 01:07:23.020
Well, they're about to really uncover some details here in this little mystery, because

1570
01:07:23.020 --> 01:07:25.920
Jim has a conversation with Kelly, and she doesn't have anything to say.

1571
01:07:26.100 --> 01:07:28.200
He literally asks her about Daryl.

1572
01:07:28.400 --> 01:07:29.760
Like, normally she'd be chatty.

1573
01:07:29.760 --> 01:07:31.480
And Pam is like, wait a second.

1574
01:07:32.140 --> 01:07:34.020
Why isn't she talking your ear off?

1575
01:07:34.300 --> 01:07:38.500
You know, it's a good thing that Pam was in Jim's ear this day, because he may have

1576
01:07:38.500 --> 01:07:40.640
never figured this out without her, truly.

1577
01:07:40.880 --> 01:07:41.160
Mm-hmm.

1578
01:07:41.360 --> 01:07:42.060
You know what I mean?

1579
01:07:42.200 --> 01:07:45.420
Well, the next scene really cracked me up, because Jim goes to Ryan.

1580
01:07:45.680 --> 01:07:47.260
Ryan's got to know what's up with Kelly, right?

1581
01:07:47.520 --> 01:07:47.820
Mm-hmm.

1582
01:07:47.820 --> 01:07:52.340
And Ryan, I fell in love with Ryan in this episode, Jenna.

1583
01:07:52.460 --> 01:07:53.440
Yeah, you're with me now!

1584
01:07:53.700 --> 01:07:58.720
I'm with you, I'm with you, because Ryan said, this made me laugh, he says, I don't

1585
01:07:58.720 --> 01:08:00.340
play the politics game anymore, Jim.

1586
01:08:00.540 --> 01:08:01.400
Can I tell you something?

1587
01:08:01.600 --> 01:08:03.620
I played it full on in New York.

1588
01:08:03.740 --> 01:08:07.200
I played it high stakes, for keeps, made it to the top.

1589
01:08:08.080 --> 01:08:09.860
Like, who is this guy?

1590
01:08:10.080 --> 01:08:12.880
And my favorite thing is, he's like, can I tell you what I learned?

1591
01:08:12.880 --> 01:08:14.480
As he takes a sip of coffee.

1592
01:08:14.700 --> 01:08:17.000
So we never end up finding out what he learned.

1593
01:08:17.080 --> 01:08:18.200
I'm so sad.

1594
01:08:18.440 --> 01:08:20.260
I would love to know his lessons.

1595
01:08:20.580 --> 01:08:22.560
But Jim sees the coffee mug.

1596
01:08:22.680 --> 01:08:22.980
Yes!

1597
01:08:23.140 --> 01:08:26.720
This is the Columbo starting to piece it together, like Stephen talked about.

1598
01:08:26.980 --> 01:08:32.620
Yes, he also has a coffee mug with his face and the little star, and that's when it becomes

1599
01:08:32.620 --> 01:08:38.280
clear that Jim and Dwight did not attend Kelly's America's Got Talent viewing party.

1600
01:08:38.540 --> 01:08:39.800
These were the party favors!

1601
01:08:40.180 --> 01:08:41.340
These were the party favors!

1602
01:08:41.340 --> 01:08:47.060
And somewhere in her house, Kelly has a mug with Dwight's face on it and Jim's.

1603
01:08:47.340 --> 01:08:49.000
She probably smashed them.

1604
01:08:49.160 --> 01:08:50.420
Oh, I didn't even think about that.

1605
01:08:50.440 --> 01:08:50.700
Oh, yeah!

1606
01:08:50.880 --> 01:08:52.160
She bought everyone mugs!

1607
01:08:52.320 --> 01:08:57.320
And so these leftover mugs are sitting there just making her so angry every day.

1608
01:08:57.460 --> 01:08:57.740
Mm-hmm.

1609
01:08:58.060 --> 01:09:02.000
And she's finally, oh, revenge is a dish best served cold, Kelly.

1610
01:09:02.180 --> 01:09:02.720
Well done!

1611
01:09:02.900 --> 01:09:03.300
I know.

1612
01:09:03.880 --> 01:09:06.220
Well, I want you to know, Jim figures it out.

1613
01:09:06.340 --> 01:09:09.540
He rushes over to Dwight and says, Dwight, you were right.

1614
01:09:09.540 --> 01:09:11.720
And I loved this scene so much.

1615
01:09:12.140 --> 01:09:14.880
Dwight is finally right about a conspiracy.

1616
01:09:15.300 --> 01:09:18.080
And then, like, a 10-year-old boy, he's like, let's go get her!

1617
01:09:18.240 --> 01:09:19.260
And Jim's like, wait!

1618
01:09:19.520 --> 01:09:22.520
But first he does that crazy air kick at Phyllis!

1619
01:09:22.540 --> 01:09:23.040
I know!

1620
01:09:23.560 --> 01:09:28.580
Well, also in that interview with Lester, he said that Rain improvised that air kick.

1621
01:09:28.700 --> 01:09:30.560
He only did it one time, but it was so brilliant.

1622
01:09:30.640 --> 01:09:31.980
That's the take they used.

1623
01:09:32.080 --> 01:09:32.840
Of course he did.

1624
01:09:32.840 --> 01:09:37.900
Because if you guys watch the show, Dwight does that air kick whenever he gets real excited.

1625
01:09:38.100 --> 01:09:41.340
He's done it in the stairwell before a big sales call.

1626
01:09:41.340 --> 01:09:42.700
It's the happy air kick.

1627
01:09:42.900 --> 01:09:43.040
Yeah.

1628
01:09:43.340 --> 01:09:44.480
I'm going to start using it.

1629
01:09:44.580 --> 01:09:45.660
Pump it up, air kick.

1630
01:09:45.860 --> 01:09:50.240
Also in that interview with Lester, he said he was really proud of this mug idea.

1631
01:09:50.580 --> 01:09:56.400
And he said that ultimately the writers knew that Kelly was going to sabotage the customer

1632
01:09:56.400 --> 01:09:59.620
surveys because Dwight and Jim skipped her viewing party.

1633
01:09:59.880 --> 01:10:04.440
But they couldn't figure out how the guys would realize this fact.

1634
01:10:04.440 --> 01:10:10.360
They had originally talked about maybe having Dwight tap Kelly's phone and overhear something.

1635
01:10:10.360 --> 01:10:14.220
Or maybe they would find like a secret recording device or something.

1636
01:10:14.460 --> 01:10:17.860
But that's when Lester got the party favor mug idea.

1637
01:10:17.900 --> 01:10:19.560
And it's really so genius.

1638
01:10:19.840 --> 01:10:24.940
And then paired with the way Stephen directed it, it's just so great.

1639
01:10:25.420 --> 01:10:28.620
Two great people working together making a great moment.

1640
01:10:28.940 --> 01:10:29.160
Yeah.

1641
01:10:29.340 --> 01:10:32.820
We also got a fan question about this scene from Evan L.

1642
01:10:32.820 --> 01:10:36.240
Did the cast do a photo shoot for the mugs?

1643
01:10:36.480 --> 01:10:41.720
And if so, did they ask you guys to make weird faces because Oscar looks really bored on his?

1644
01:10:42.760 --> 01:10:44.940
I don't remember a special photo shoot.

1645
01:10:45.060 --> 01:10:46.900
We had done a publicity photo shoot.

1646
01:10:46.980 --> 01:10:48.940
So maybe they use those images.

1647
01:10:48.940 --> 01:10:51.440
But I'm looking at my face on the mug right now.

1648
01:10:51.560 --> 01:10:55.560
And it's also possible that Phil just walked around and snapped pictures of us.

1649
01:10:55.700 --> 01:10:59.840
It kind of looks like one of your publicity photos that maybe they color enhanced.

1650
01:11:00.260 --> 01:11:01.740
I still have my publicity photo.

1651
01:11:01.740 --> 01:11:03.620
So do you want me to do a side-by-side in stories?

1652
01:11:03.900 --> 01:11:04.220
Yes.

1653
01:11:04.360 --> 01:11:05.040
We'll vote, guys.

1654
01:11:05.180 --> 01:11:06.280
Do you think it's the same picture?

1655
01:11:06.420 --> 01:11:08.880
Or do you think Phil just took my picture at my desk one day?

1656
01:11:08.980 --> 01:11:10.180
Because they did do that sometimes.

1657
01:11:10.540 --> 01:11:10.800
Oh, they would.

1658
01:11:10.960 --> 01:11:14.600
They would walk around and you'd just be sitting there and they'd snap a picture of you for something.

1659
01:11:14.820 --> 01:11:16.100
We'll get to the bottom of it.

1660
01:11:16.440 --> 01:11:19.020
Well, Jenna, Kelly's going to get called into Michael's office.

1661
01:11:19.040 --> 01:11:19.440
Mm-hmm.

1662
01:11:19.700 --> 01:11:21.320
And she's busted now.

1663
01:11:21.500 --> 01:11:22.080
She is.

1664
01:11:22.280 --> 01:11:23.520
Dwight wants her fired.

1665
01:11:23.760 --> 01:11:24.060
Yeah.

1666
01:11:24.360 --> 01:11:26.200
And Michael asks them to leave the office.

1667
01:11:26.420 --> 01:11:27.620
You know, he's like, this is serious.

1668
01:11:27.620 --> 01:11:28.820
I need you to leave the office.

1669
01:11:29.140 --> 01:11:32.440
And then Michael says this, and I loved it so much.

1670
01:11:32.560 --> 01:11:39.440
Michael says, I have an enormous amount of trouble trying to get people to come to my place.

1671
01:11:39.560 --> 01:11:40.520
And I hate it.

1672
01:11:40.680 --> 01:11:44.620
I can't tell you how much leftover guacamole I've ended up eating over the years.

1673
01:11:44.840 --> 01:11:47.280
I don't even know why I make it in such great quantities.

1674
01:11:47.880 --> 01:11:50.920
And then he says, listen, just sit there and pretend to cry, right?

1675
01:11:51.060 --> 01:11:51.680
Can you do that?

1676
01:11:51.820 --> 01:11:51.920
Yeah.

1677
01:11:51.920 --> 01:11:55.120
And then they both end up laughing, and it's a really sweet moment.

1678
01:11:55.340 --> 01:11:56.180
It really is.

1679
01:11:56.340 --> 01:12:04.960
And we got a bunch of people writing in to ask if that laugh after Kelly fake cries, if that was like a fake laugh or if Mindy broke.

1680
01:12:05.360 --> 01:12:07.060
No, that was scripted.

1681
01:12:07.200 --> 01:12:10.500
It's scripted that her fake crying made them laugh.

1682
01:12:10.700 --> 01:12:11.860
Well, I'll say this.

1683
01:12:11.940 --> 01:12:20.340
In re-watching this episode, like three times, right, before today, I could hear Mindy's fake laugh and then her real laugh.

1684
01:12:20.460 --> 01:12:20.780
Yeah.

1685
01:12:20.780 --> 01:12:28.880
So if you watch it, she fake cries, she fake laughs, then Steve laughs as Michael, and then Mindy laughs as herself.

1686
01:12:29.060 --> 01:12:29.220
Yeah.

1687
01:12:29.420 --> 01:12:31.280
Her real laugh definitely comes out.

1688
01:12:31.460 --> 01:12:31.620
Yeah.

1689
01:12:31.800 --> 01:12:39.180
So now we're at this scene at Corporate, which we talked about a lot with Stephen, this scene where Alex comes to Pam's work.

1690
01:12:39.280 --> 01:12:42.260
He's going to kidnap her, wants to see this art.

1691
01:12:42.420 --> 01:12:44.540
He said wine and cheese, okay?

1692
01:12:45.180 --> 01:12:46.480
That's all you got to hear.

1693
01:12:46.920 --> 01:12:47.400
Midday.

1694
01:12:47.400 --> 01:12:50.400
Midday, there's an exhibit with wine and cheese.

1695
01:12:50.600 --> 01:12:51.880
That's not being friends.

1696
01:12:52.360 --> 01:12:52.700
Yeah.

1697
01:12:53.040 --> 01:12:58.820
Well, thanks to James-a-pedia, I saw all of the candy bag for this.

1698
01:12:59.200 --> 01:13:00.580
How many were there?

1699
01:13:00.740 --> 01:13:01.100
Ten.

1700
01:13:01.340 --> 01:13:03.040
Ten alts for this scene.

1701
01:13:03.100 --> 01:13:03.380
Yes.

1702
01:13:03.680 --> 01:13:04.720
Oh, my word.

1703
01:13:04.840 --> 01:13:04.980
Yeah.

1704
01:13:04.980 --> 01:13:09.300
I wanted to count because we kind of talked about it, and it was ten.

1705
01:13:09.480 --> 01:13:14.580
Ten alternate scenes, and I swear we shot so many, so many versions of it.

1706
01:13:14.700 --> 01:13:17.060
And I remember doing these scenes with Rich.

1707
01:13:17.160 --> 01:13:18.840
It was so grueling.

1708
01:13:18.940 --> 01:13:20.420
And we really bonded.

1709
01:13:20.760 --> 01:13:26.980
Like, Rich and I are great friends today, I think, because we went through this moment together.

1710
01:13:26.980 --> 01:13:29.620
Yeah, you were in the trenches of trying to find this scene.

1711
01:13:29.780 --> 01:13:30.020
Yes.

1712
01:13:30.220 --> 01:13:32.320
Well, we should have Rich on and talk about it.

1713
01:13:32.420 --> 01:13:33.820
We need to hear his side of things.

1714
01:13:33.940 --> 01:13:34.220
We do.

1715
01:13:34.300 --> 01:13:35.480
Of shooting this crazy scene.

1716
01:13:35.640 --> 01:13:36.160
Let's call him.

1717
01:13:36.240 --> 01:13:36.800
Rich, come on.

1718
01:13:37.260 --> 01:13:41.820
So, I feel like we really covered this, but we did have a fan write in, and I'm so sorry

1719
01:13:41.820 --> 01:13:44.900
I didn't write down your name because I thought this was a really good observation.

1720
01:13:45.340 --> 01:13:51.740
They were saying, wasn't Pam's art program three months long, and she went at the beginning

1721
01:13:51.740 --> 01:13:52.340
